NAME
    rmdir - remove empty directories

SYNOPSIS
    rmdir DIRECTORY...

DESCRIPTION
    Removes each empty writable directory operand. Nonempty directories, roots,
    mountpoints, read-only objects, files, and symbolic links are rejected.

    Every operand is attempted. A nonempty directory is reported and the
    remaining operands are still removed; the exit status reflects the first
    failure.

    rmdir is not a restricted spelling of rm -r. It refuses a nonempty
    directory, which is the reason to reach for it when a directory is only
    expected to be empty.

EXAMPLES
    rmdir /vol/shared/empty
    rmdir stage-*
